lazysite (0.7.5-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * New binary packages lazysite-apache and lazysite-nginx (the SM139
    webserver glue): commented vhost examples for both runtime patterns
    on each server - plain CGI (Apache FallbackResource / nginx
    try_files + fcgiwrap through the CGI auth wrapper) and the per-site
    FastCGI pool (mod_proxy_fcgi / native fastcgi_pass to
    /run/lazysite/<domain>.sock, session-bearing requests carved out to
    the CGI auth wrapper) - plus lazysite-apache-vhost and
    lazysite-nginx-vhost (add/remove): root-run render commands writing
    sites-available/<domain>.conf that never touch site content and
    print, never run, the enable/reload steps.
  * New `lazysite demo` verb (lazysite-common): zero-argument try-it -
    fresh-installs a scratch site (default ~/lazysite-demo) as the
    current user, never root, and serves it on the built-in dev server.
  * docs/reference/webserver-wiring.md: one wiring reference for every
    front-end - the two runtime patterns explained once, per-server
    sections for Apache/nginx (the glue packages) plus Caddy and
    lighttpd snippets, and the generic front-end contract; shipped in
    both glue packages' doc directories.

 -- Stuart J. Mackintosh <sjm@opendigital.cc>  Sat, 11 Jul 2026 09:00:00 +0100

